  <page>
    <title>Porto Ottiolu</title>
    <id>25133</id>
    <revision>
      <id>15921805</id>
      <timestamp>2005-05-12T16:25:54Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>Nabla</username>
        <id>90397</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>cped + {{Italy-geo-stub}}</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Porto Ottiolu''' is a private [[marina]] and a touristic destination located in [[Sardinia]], [[Italy]], on [[Tyrrhenian Sea]], some 35 km south of [[Olbia]].

It was built in [[1988]] in the place in where was once the ancient [[Rome|Roman]] port of ''Portiolum,'' and after its immediate success, a huge village was built around it with the same name.

The marina can host 405 boats in 8 classes and has complete services. It is the largestmarina of the East coast of Sardinia.

In its waters, [[apnea|apneist]] diver [[Gianluca Genoni]] repeatedly scored new world records.

Other activities include fishing.

{{Italy-geo-stub}}</text>
    </revision>
