      <text xml:space="preserve">{{wiktionary|queen}}

The word '''''Queen''''' ultimately derives from an Indo-European root ''*gwena'' (woman) via Old English ''cwén'' (woman, wife, queen). ''Cf.'' Old Norse ''kvenna'' (woman), Gothic ''qens'' (wife), Greek ''gynē'' (woman), Russian ''zhena'', Sanskrit ''jani''. It has many meanings:
__NOTOC__
==Political==
* [[Queen regnant]], a female monarch
* [[Queen consort]], the wife of a king
* [[Queen dowager]], a woman who was queen consort but whose husband has died or abdicated, someone else having become monarch
* [[Queen Mother]], a queen dowager whose child, having succeeded his or her father, is now the monarch
* [[Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom|Her Majesty Queen Elizabeth II of the United Kingdom]] [http://www.royal.gov.uk]
* [[Margrethe II of Denmark|Her Majesty Queen Margrethe II of Denmark]] [http://www.kongehuset.dk/english/]
* [[Beatrix of the Netherlands| Her Majesty Queen Beatrix of the Netherlands]]

==Biology==
* [[Queen (insect)]], the only female insect in a hive or colony of social insects that is fertile and egg laying
* [[Queen (cat)]], a female cat, usually one with a litter of kittens
* [[Queen (butterfly)]], a butterfly species from the subfamily ''Danainae'' found in North America
* [[Queen bee]], the only female honeybee in a hive that is fertile and egg laying

==Game and sport==
* [[Queen (chess)]], the most powerful piece in the game of chess
* [[Queen (chess engine)]], the name of a chess engine
* [[Queen (playing card)]], a card in a deck of playing cards or tarot cards
* [[Promotion (chess)|Queening]], an act in the game of checkers, draughts, or chess
* [[Queen's Club]] tennis club in London and the annual tennis tournament held there

==Art and literature==
* [[Queen (band)]], a British rock band, most prolific in the 1970s and 1980s
* [[Queen (album)|''Queen'' (album)]], the band Queen's debut album
* ''[[Queen: The Story of an American Family]]'', a book by Alex Haley and a 1993 TV-miniseries based on the book

==Other==
* [[Queen Latifah]], an actress and singer
* [[Drag queen]], a type of entertainer
* [[Prom queen]]
* &quot;[[Queen's Scout]] Award&quot;, the highest youth award in scouting when the British monarch is a female
* [[The Virgin Mary]], as known by several epithets, including &quot;Queen of the World,&quot; &quot;Queen of Heaven,&quot; and &quot;Queen of Angels&quot;
* [[Facesitting]] or &quot;queening&quot;, a sex act

==See also==
*[[Queen of Farts]]
*[[Queens]], a borough in New York City, New York
*[[Queen's University, Canada]], a university in Kingston, Ontario, Canada
*[[Queens County, New Brunswick]]
*[[Queens County, Nova Scotia]]
*[[Queens County, Prince Edward Island]]
*[[Queen's (electoral district)]], a disambiguation page for several electoral districts named Queens and Queen's in Canada
*[[Queens' College, Cambridge]]


