  <page>
    <title>Quadrillion</title>
    <id>25218</id>
    <revision>
      <id>36404887</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-23T21:03:05Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>128.252.121.2</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* Properties */ don't see the relevance of 255-gons.</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">The '''quadrillion''' is a large [[number]] which has one of two values depending on how or where it is being used. Quadrillion comes after [[trillion]]. 

== Short scale usage ==
In [[long and short scales|short scale]] usage, a '''quadrillion''' is equal to a 1 with 15 zeroes, namely:
1,000,000,000,000,000 ([[1 E15|10&lt;sup&gt;15&lt;/sup&gt;]])

It is a thousand trillion (short scale), i.e. a thousand million million. The [[SI prefix]] for this number is [[peta]].

== Long scale usage ==
In [[long and short scales|long scale]] usage, a '''quadrillion''' is equal to a 1 with 24 zeroes, namely:
1,000,000,000,000,000,000,000,000 ([[1 E24|10&lt;sup&gt;24&lt;/sup&gt;]])

It is a thousand sextillion (short scale), The SI prefix for this number is [[yotta]].

While people in the [[British Isles]], [[Australia]] and [[New Zealand]] traditionally employed the long scale usage, they have largely switched to the short scale usage.

==Properties==
Quadrillion is the lowest natural number with a &quot;q&quot; in its name. A quadrillion has 255 proper divisors.  The [[divisor function]] calculated on a quadrillion is equal to:

: &lt;math&gt; \sigma(10^{15})\;=\;2,499,961,853,010,960&lt;/math&gt;

and therefore its [[Abundant number|abundancy]] is 499,961,853,010,960, which is almost half of a quadrillion.
The divisor function of a quadrillion (and indeed, of all high powers of ten) may be calculated with the formula:

: &lt;math&gt; \sigma(10^n)\;=\;\frac{(2^{n+1} - 1)(5^{n+1} - 1)}{4}&lt;/math&gt;

which may be seen by applying the formula for the partial sum of a [[geometric series]] twice to the sum of the divisors.

== See also ==
*[[List of numbers]]
*[[Names of large numbers]]

[[Category:Integers]]
[[Category:Large numbers]]

[[it:Quadrilione]]
[[pl:Kwadrylion]]
[[fi:Kvadriljoona]]</text>
